course: dictionary
lesson: 3283
title: A French word in English
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are borrowed from other languages and keep their original spelling. «Escargot» is a French word, and English menus and cookbooks use it when they mean a snail cooked to be eaten.
explain: Read the words around it to find its meaning. «Les escargots are snails cooked in garlic butter, a famous dish many French children eat only on special occasions.» The clues garlic butter and dish tell you it is food, and snails tells you what kind of food.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Snails cooked in garlic butter» still makes sense, so escargot means a snail cooked to be eaten. Words from other languages often come with helpful clues, such as «Non merci», which is a polite way to say no.
fact: Escargot is a French word, and English uses it too.
fact: «Escargot» means a snail cooked to be eaten, usually with garlic butter.
fact: In French, «escargot» is simply the everyday word for snail.
fact: Say it like «ess-car-GO», with the t silent.
fact: «Non merci» is a polite way to say no.
exercise: «Les escargots are snails cooked in garlic butter, a famous dish.» What does escargot mean here? | A small French car | A type of garlic bread | A kind of butter | *A snail cooked to be eaten
exercise: The word «escargot» comes from which language? | Spanish | *French | German | Italian
exercise: On an English menu, what would «escargots» most likely be? | *Snails cooked to eat | Soup with peas | Fresh bread | Cheese
test: «Many French children eat escargots only on special occasions.» What does this tell you about escargots? | *They are a special treat food | They are cheap sandwiches | They are eaten every single day | They are only for animals
test: A friend says «Non merci» when offered escargots. What is she doing? | Ordering a drink | *Politely saying no | Saying yes very loudly | Asking for more
exam: What is the best way to check your guess about the meaning of escargot? | Skip the sentence forever | Ask someone to draw a picture of it | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Count the letters in the word
